# 🚀 Server Setup & n8n Workflow Guide

Use this guide to host your backend on an AWS T3 Small server (Ubuntu) and configure the automation.

---

## Part 1: Linux Server Setup (AWS)

Connect to your server via SSH and run the following commands block by block.

### 1. Install Docker & Dependencies
```bash
# Update System
sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y

# Install Docker and Docker Compose
sudo apt install -y docker.io docker-compose

# Enable Docker to run on startup
sudo systemctl enable --now docker

# Allow your user to run docker commands without sudo
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
newgrp docker
```

### 2. Set Up Cloudflare Tunnel
This exposes your local n8n to the web securely (https) without opening ports.

```bash
# Download and install Cloudflared
curl -L --output cloudflared.deb https://github.com/cloudflare/cloudflared/releases/latest/download/cloudflared-linux-amd64.deb
sudo dpkg -i cloudflared.deb

# Login to Cloudflare (Copy the URL provided to your browser)
cloudflared tunnel login

# Create a new tunnel named 'n8n-tunnel'
cloudflared tunnel create n8n-tunnel

# Route the tunnel to your domain (Replace api.yourdomain.com)
cloudflared tunnel route dns n8n-tunnel api.yourdomain.com
```

### 3. Deploy n8n Container
Create the folder and configuration.

```bash
mkdir n8n-server
cd n8n-server
nano docker-compose.yml
```

**Paste the following into `docker-compose.yml`:**

```yaml
version: "3"
services:
  n8n:
    image: n8nio/n8n
    restart: always
    ports:
      - "5678:5678"
    environment:
      - N8N_HOST=api.yourdomain.com
      - N8N_PORT=5678
      - N8N_PROTOCOL=https
      - WEBHOOK_URL=https://api.yourdomain.com/
      - GENERIC_TIMEZONE=UTC
    volumes:
      - ./n8n_data:/home/node/.n8n
```

**Start the server:**
```bash
docker-compose up -d
```

### 4. Run the Tunnel
Keep the tunnel running to accept traffic.
```bash
# Run in background (using nohup or systemd is recommended for production)
cloudflared tunnel run n8n-tunnel
```

